  "outcomes": [
    "Optional mill validates the complete sampled nonnegative land count; insufficient libraries cannot accept, zero is legal, and quantities sample at resolution. Source-power attack mill uses current exact-source power or final departure LKI, floored at zero; optional target omission mills nobody.",
    "Ainok-shaped mill/recovery uses exact public post-mill incarnations, including exile redirection. Choosing recovery skips the fallback under CR118.12; decline or no eligible land puts a counter on the exact live source.",
    "Independent legal creature targets retain their separate effects. Graveyard creature power is captured before return changes a CDA; illegal graveyard targets supply no damage amount. Both targets remain mandatory at announcement.",
    "Token-qualified bounce captures legal token status before movement, draws for tokens only, and respects optional omission/stale incarnation. Ordinary token creation uses the exact-recipe staged entry path.",
    "Actual remembered draws use the existing packet-owned DrawRequest continuation, including private miracle interruptions; a qualifying any-kind counter permits the draw, and no completed draw runs the fallback independently of earlier turn draws.",
    "One explicit damage batch carries its owning packet id through replacements. Only actual positive player damage marks discard recipients; permanent damage and prevented damage do not discard, while life gain remains independent. Replacement order and recipient discard choices survive raw/index branching and restore.",
    "Yathan-shaped mandatory mill always mills available cards. Its exact-four reflexive packet is queued after completed milling, so targets are selected after the event. Public exile redirection counts as milling; RevealShuffleSelf with no library departure is excluded under CR614.6/701.17c. This replacement distinction is a reasoned CR inference; official Yathan notes explicitly say mill four but do not separately address Progenitus."
  ],
